\description{
Each row is a report of four of dansk_planted's vessels, at 1 min and 6 min, faults and all, written through one of eight clocks or streams (the fix's own time, cut or rounded to the minute, jittered, stamped on receipt, an hourly stream beside, resampled with fills, a derived speed), with new faults of position, time and speed; every row holds the report as written and as it truly was, and what an ideal flagger does with it, for scoring a flagger on both kinds of error. Read it with \code{rb_read_example("dansk_truth")}.
}
\details{
dansk_planted's vessels EX_6, EX_10, EX_12 and EX_14 at 1 min and 6 min, each track copied once per clock (\code{clock}): the fix's own time; every time cut, or rounded, to its minute (a ping dropped where two land on one minute); a third of the times written up to half a step off; two streams, the fix's time and the time received (1-90 s late, drifting), a report in both a copy; an hourly stream beside the track, its clock 0-120 s ahead; the track at the minute with stretches of 3-10 fixes lost and filled along straight lines; the speed derived from the positions. Planted besides: five pings before a silence moved 2-10 km together (relocation), a ping written late (late_stamp), a speed report of 60 kn (speed_glitch), and a filled stretch drawn to a misplaced fix (misplaced_fill) (\code{data-raw/truth.R}, a fixed seed). A track is one \code{vid}: the vessel, the rate and the clock.
}
